{"reference": "C", "saved_D_answer": "C", "saved_D_rationale": "Answer: C\nReason: The chest X-ray demonstrates multiple bilateral pulmonary nodules of varying sizes, some with ill-defined margins suggestive of cavitation or necrosis. In a patient presenting with chest pain and non-productive cough, this radiographic pattern is characteristic of Necrotizing Sarcoid Granulomatosis (NSG), a rare variant of sarcoidosis that mimics malignancy or vasculitis but fits the specific \"necrotizing\" nodule description often tested in this context."}
